@meta
id: 06-04
title: The end of the text, not the line
chapter: 06
type: lesson
skills: line-end
par: 48
minutes: 4
vscode: End, then backspace over invisible spaces
open: refunds.csv

@brief
Three rows exported out of the finance spreadsheet. Each one has picked up
stray spaces on the end during the copy, which you cannot see but which are
really there.

Every row needs a new final column recording who approved it:

    ord_1042,cus_88,4999,GBP,APPROVED,finance

Append `,finance` to all three rows. It has to sit directly against the
status, not out past the invisible spaces, or the field will be read as
`APPROVED   ` and no lookup will match it.

@keys
| `$` | the last character, spaces included |
| `g_` | the last character that is not a space or tab |
| `a` | insert to the right of the cursor |

@hints
`$` and `A` both go past the stray spaces, which is exactly the wrong place.
You want the mirror image of `^`.
--
`g_` — a `g` then an underscore — lands on the last non-blank character of
the line. Press `a` there and your text goes right after the status.
--
`g_`, `a`, type `,finance`, `Esc`, then `j` and the same again for each row.

@solution
    g_ a ,finance <Esc> j g_ a ,finance <Esc> j g_ a ,finance <Esc> :wq<Enter>

`g_` is `^` seen from the other end: the last character that is actually
text. On a tidy line it does the same job as `$`, and the two only part
company when there is trailing whitespace — which, in real files that have
been through a spreadsheet, an email client or a badly configured editor,
there often is.

The wider lesson is that `$` is a position on a line and `g_` is a position
in the content, and the two are not the same claim. When you are appending
to data you almost always mean the content.

The stray spaces themselves are left alone here. Nothing in this chapter
deletes text yet; chapter 8 gives you `d`, and `dg_` reads as delete to the
last real character, which is when this key starts to pay properly.

@start refunds.csv
ord_1042,cus_88,4999,GBP,APPROVED   
ord_1043,cus_91,1250,GBP,DECLINED  
ord_1044,cus_88,899,GBP,APPROVED    

@expected refunds.csv
ord_1042,cus_88,4999,GBP,APPROVED,finance
ord_1043,cus_91,1250,GBP,DECLINED,finance
ord_1044,cus_88,899,GBP,APPROVED,finance
